{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00661",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 13.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.24,
      "text": "Hello again, doctor. I know it's only a cough, but it's been going on for three weeks now and it's driving me round the bend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.13,
      "end_seconds": 24.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Not just a cough if it's driven you in. Tell me what it's like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.6,
      "end_seconds": 43.69,
      "duration_seconds": 17.09,
      "text": "Dry, tickly, mostly. It starts as soon as I lie down at night, and I'm getting no sleep. Oh, and sometimes I cough so hard I feel sick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.3,
      "end_seconds": 48.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "And it began with a cold?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.42,
      "end_seconds": 57.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "A bad cold, yes, three weeks ago. The cold went, but the cough stayed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.49,
      "end_seconds": 63.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Any fever, or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.92,
      "end_seconds": 68.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No fever, no blood. Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.78,
      "end_seconds": 74.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Weight loss, sweats at night, anything of that kind?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.63,
      "end_seconds": 82.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "No, I've actually put on a bit of weight, sadly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.48,
      "end_seconds": 88.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Good. Let's check what you take regularly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.34,
      "end_seconds": 99.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "The ramipril, 5 mg once a day, for my blood pressure, and metformin, 500 mg twice a day. That's it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.54,
      "end_seconds": 109.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "And remind me of your other conditions, apart from the blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.79,
      "end_seconds": 119.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "I've got type 2 diabetes, and I had asthma as a child, but I grew out of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.98,
      "end_seconds": 127.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "I see. Let me check your temperature, pulse and oxygen. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.97,
      "end_seconds": 131.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.48,
      "end_seconds": 150.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Temperature 36.7, pulse 76, oxygen 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.42,
      "end_seconds": 156.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "All fine, I suppose. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.98,
      "end_seconds": 185.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "All fine. Breathe in and out for me, normally. I'm listening to your chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.24,
      "end_seconds": 189.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Is it clear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.88,
      "end_seconds": 212.69,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "Your chest is clear, no crackles and no wheeze. Open wide. Your throat is a bit red at the back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.58,
      "end_seconds": 219.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "So what's wrong with me? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.07,
      "end_seconds": 234.03,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "After a cold, it's common for the airways to stay twitchy for weeks, so I think this is most likely a post-viral cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.96,
      "end_seconds": 240.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Right. How long will it go on? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.16,
      "end_seconds": 262.25,
      "duration_seconds": 19.09,
      "text": "It can last up to eight weeks. But there's one other thing. Ramipril, your blood pressure tablet, can itself cause a dry, tickly cough in some people, so I can't rule out a side effect of the ramipril."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.5,
      "end_seconds": 271.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "Oh! I never thought of that. I've been on it for years. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.19,
      "end_seconds": 283.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "Sometimes it starts late. I wouldn't stop it yet, but let's keep it in mind. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.75,
      "end_seconds": 289.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "What do we do now? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.62,
      "end_seconds": 304.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "Because it's been three weeks, I'd like to do a chest X-ray, to be sure there's nothing in the lungs. And a spirometry test to check your airways."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.44,
      "end_seconds": 309.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "And bloods? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.0,
      "end_seconds": 320.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "Yes, a blood test as well, to check your blood count and sugar control while we're at it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.31,
      "end_seconds": 327.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Fine. And what do I do about the cough? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.35,
      "end_seconds": 339.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.88,
      "text": "Honey and warm water at night can soothe the throat, and propping up on an extra pillow helps with lying down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.74,
      "end_seconds": 344.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I'll try the honey. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.87,
      "end_seconds": 358.38,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the results, and we'll decide about the ramipril then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.78,
      "end_seconds": 363.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Three weeks. Thanks, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
